WEBVTT

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:16.600
<i>Along a zigzag the world turns,</i>
<i>I heave out a sigh.</i>

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:27.610
<i>Someone pauses along the way,</i>
<i>but reality moves on.</i>

00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:33.150
<i>Treat love as love, treat</i>
<i>dreams as dreams.</i>

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:38.650
<i>It's difficult to say it in earnest.</i>
<i>The times forge ahead, but...</i>

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:43.630
<i>I want to make you happy...</i>

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:49.360
<i>I'll do so like I do to</i>
<i>be myself. Yeah!</i>

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:54.400
<i>I'll make you happy...</i>

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:59.810
<i>I dedicate all that</i>
<i>I can do to you.</i>

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:11.130
<i>Along a zigzag the world turns,</i>
<i>I heave out a sigh.</i>

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:23.370
<i>Someone pauses along the way,</i>
<i>but love doesn't stop for me.</i>

00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:31.110
FILE. 8
BIG DUEL FOR
LUCKY YORIKO

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:48.090
How are you
doing?

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:50.230
Oh... Almost
done.

00:01:51.530 --> 00:01:53.500
Jeez, this
is awful!

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:54.900
What's the matter?

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:56.630
What's the matter?
Come take a look at this!

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:00.800
A serious offender...

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:02.580
What shall we do?

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:04.740
What shall we do?
Let's just wait a bit.

00:02:04.910 --> 00:02:08.580
Maybe there's some reason
they couldn't move the car.

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:20.830
Yoriko, you're too soft!
You're WAY too easy!

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:21.930
Huh?

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:25.060
If you can't punish those
who break the law...

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:27.660
...then you're not qualified
to do police work...

00:02:27.770 --> 00:02:29.360
...eh, Yoriko Nikaidou?

00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:39.770
Long time no see! I haven't see you since
the academy! How've you been?

00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:42.810
Oh, just great! Yeah! How
about yourself?

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:44.650
Hey, stop
that!

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:47.080
I didn't come here to get
all mushy with you!

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:47.880
Oh.

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:49.650
Who's she?

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:54.060
My roommate from the academy...
Chie Sagami-Ono.

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:56.860
Really? Nice
to meet you.

00:02:57.030 --> 00:03:00.300
How do you do? The pleasure's
all mine, I'm sure.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:04.230
Oops. Did it again. Will you people
just stop with the pleasantries?!

00:03:04.770 --> 00:03:08.260
Yoriko! I came here
to challenge you!

00:03:09.110 --> 00:03:11.740
Challenge me?! Me?

00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:15.040
How come? What did
I ever do to you?

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:18.720
What did you do? Hard to believe
you can play so innocent...

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:20.650
...considering you
ruined my life!

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:23.450
Yoriko, what on earth
did you do to her?!

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:26.560
People don't get this upset unless
you've done something awful.

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:30.390
Hmm... But I really haven't
the faintest idea.

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:34.700
Hmph! You graduated with
higher marks than I did.

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:37.500
Still gonna play
dumb with me?

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:40.270
You got lower marks than Yoriko
at the police academy?

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:46.110
Tell me, does that mean you're challenging
everyone from your class...

00:03:46.210 --> 00:03:47.680
...with better grades
than you?

00:03:47.850 --> 00:03:51.810
Everyone? Yoriko was the
only one who beat me.

00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:53.710
Huh?!

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:58.020
So, Yoriko, that means you were the
top graduate at the academy?

00:04:00.190 --> 00:04:01.290
No way!

00:04:01.460 --> 00:04:03.300
Way to go, Yoriko!

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:04.530
It was nothing.

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:08.400
That's right. It was a total fluke! She
lucked her way into first place.

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:10.340
Hey, watch it!

00:04:10.340 --> 00:04:12.100
Forget it, Natsumi.

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:13.900
She's absolutely right.

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:20.210
Excuse me. Exactly how has losing to
Yoriko completely ruined your life?

00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:22.280
Could you explain
that to me?

00:04:26.590 --> 00:04:31.620
It's like this... Ever since I was born,
I've always been number one.

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:37.420
When I was a baby, I won the National
Healthy Baby Contest.

00:04:37.530 --> 00:04:41.900
In the kindergarten plays, I was
always a beautiful princess.

00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:44.500
Not to mention the fact that I always
got top marks in school.

00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:46.900
"#1; Sagami-Ono, Chie"

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:50.910
I received accolades for my
violin performances.

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:54.470
And in ballet, I was
the prima ballerina.

00:04:58.420 --> 00:05:00.350
I was absolutely
brilliant.

00:05:01.490 --> 00:05:03.260
What'd she come here for, anyway?

00:05:03.260 --> 00:05:05.590
What'd she come here for, anyway?
To brag about herself, it seems.

00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:08.860
The world revolved
around me!

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:11.860
Until she came
along!

00:05:18.470 --> 00:05:21.740
She couldn't even keep her eyes open,
yet every shot hit the bull's-eye!

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:25.240
<i>"Hey! Look</i>
<i>at that!"</i>

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:32.220
<i>"Whoa!"</i>

00:05:32.390 --> 00:05:35.880
In Judo, her foot slipped and
she accidentally threw me!

00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:40.180
<i>"Woo! I did that?!"</i>

00:05:48.170 --> 00:05:50.540
Even in exams, it was
fluke after fluke!

00:05:50.970 --> 00:05:53.370
<i>"Lucky me!"</i>

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:54.840
<i>"I don't believe you!"</i>

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:01.550
You mean your marks
really were a fluke?

00:06:03.020 --> 00:06:05.180
Yeah, but...

00:06:05.350 --> 00:06:10.220
If Yoriko hadn't been there, I would've
graduated at the top of the class!

00:06:10.590 --> 00:06:13.960
But it doesn't really matter how you
did while you were at the academy.

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:18.650
After all, you've become a
fine policewoman, right?

00:06:19.570 --> 00:06:24.160
I didn't join the police force because
I wanted to become a policewoman!

00:06:24.340 --> 00:06:25.900
Then why did
you join?

00:06:26.340 --> 00:06:30.800
Why else? I wanted to make
my big debut in society!

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:32.680
"Society?"

00:06:32.850 --> 00:06:35.510
Chie's the only daughter of the owner
of a certain mega-corporation.

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:37.320
"...ass monkey" Corporation?

00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:39.080
A CERTAIN mega-corporation.

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:42.280
Anyway, what do you mean you joined
the force to make your big debut?

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:50.460
I doubt anyone debuting can claim "Police
Academy, top of class" on her resume.

00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:53.530
I figured it would guarantee that all
the men would be interested in me.

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:56.030
So you joined the
police academy...

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:59.230
...in preparation
for marriage.

00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:02.030
"Marriage?"

00:07:03.140 --> 00:07:05.110
Bang!

00:07:06.150 --> 00:07:08.740
"That young princess
can shoot a gun."

00:07:08.850 --> 00:07:10.940
Dangerous, yet appealing!
Don't you think?

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:12.920
"Dangerous, yet appealing..."

00:07:12.920 --> 00:07:15.790
Well, dangerous, anyway.

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:19.690
And, the one who shattered my plans
was none other than Yoriko!

00:07:20.060 --> 00:07:23.090
I'm going to get back at you. And I'm
going to take back what I've lost!

00:07:24.100 --> 00:07:25.290
Chie!

00:07:25.470 --> 00:07:29.060
But what station has patrol
cars like this in their fleet?

00:07:29.370 --> 00:07:32.240
I've nicknamed my Porsche
patrol car "Por-Pat."

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:35.270
My father donated
it to my station...

00:07:35.380 --> 00:07:37.240
...for my exclusive use
as a patrol car.

00:07:37.340 --> 00:07:41.250
Oh, yes. Of course, I'll give you
a handicap for the race.

00:07:41.550 --> 00:07:44.710
After all, you just have one of those
"common" patrol cars, right?

00:07:45.550 --> 00:07:47.450
You want to race with
the patrol cars?

00:07:47.620 --> 00:07:51.320
We have more than "common" patrol cars!
Our station has an incredible patrol car!

00:07:51.630 --> 00:07:53.530
"An incredible
patrol car?"

00:07:53.630 --> 00:07:55.930
Oh, come to think of it,
I've heard about it.

00:07:56.030 --> 00:08:00.360
Yeah, a weird car that someone at
the Bokuto Station hotrodded.

00:08:03.270 --> 00:08:05.500
Is that the one
you mean?

00:08:05.610 --> 00:08:07.470
I'm sure I also
heard...

00:08:07.570 --> 00:08:10.540
...that one of the officers using that car
was a superhuman gorilla-woman.

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:14.040
"Superhuman gorilla-woman?!"

00:08:14.250 --> 00:08:17.440
The race will be one week from
today. We'll meet right here.

00:08:17.550 --> 00:08:18.780
Understand, Yoriko?

00:08:18.950 --> 00:08:20.250
Uh... uh...

00:08:20.420 --> 00:08:23.290
And don't forget to bring your
"incredible patrol car!"

00:08:37.770 --> 00:08:41.670
Well! Let's hurry back to the
station and finish up!

00:08:41.780 --> 00:08:44.210
What? What's with
you two?!

00:08:44.380 --> 00:08:47.110
Yoriko! Aren't you the least bit upset
about what she said about you?

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:49.040
I sure would be!

00:08:49.220 --> 00:08:50.650
No, not especially.

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:53.380
I think we know...

00:08:53.490 --> 00:08:56.080
Considering we're dear friends of yours.
Considering we're dear friends of yours.

00:08:56.260 --> 00:09:00.020
Sagami-Ono and I are friends. And
we're both police officers!

00:09:00.390 --> 00:09:03.890
Exactly! That's why
you're really upset!

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:05.030
Um... Yeah...

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:10.530
Come on, come
on! Yeah!

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:16.400
Whoa!

00:09:23.180 --> 00:09:26.150
No matter how much I've hotrodded this
car, it won't make any difference...

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:28.690
...if you don't know how to take full
advantage of its capabilities.

00:09:28.790 --> 00:09:34.060
And that means learning hands-on
what the car's limitations are.

00:09:37.560 --> 00:09:39.290
Sharp turn
to the left!

00:09:41.370 --> 00:09:42.930
Sharp turn to
the right!

00:09:46.410 --> 00:09:47.340
Brake spin!

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:56.310
I go to amusement parks
all the time, but...

00:09:56.420 --> 00:10:00.510
...l've never heard anyone scream like
that! Even on the roller coasters!

00:10:00.690 --> 00:10:04.990
Compared to Miyuki at full throttle,
a coaster is like a walk in the park.

00:10:11.800 --> 00:10:12.800
How'd she do?

00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:13.990
How'd she do?
She gonna make it?

00:10:14.170 --> 00:10:17.140
Nope. Take a look
for yourself.

00:10:19.870 --> 00:10:21.860
"Bokuto Police Station"

00:10:21.940 --> 00:10:25.210
One! Two!

00:10:25.710 --> 00:10:30.380
Three! Four!

00:10:30.650 --> 00:10:35.710
Five! Six!

00:10:35.890 --> 00:10:40.990
Seven! Eight!

00:10:41.860 --> 00:10:47.030
Nine! Ten!

00:10:48.600 --> 00:10:50.000
I can't do this
anymore!

00:10:50.170 --> 00:10:52.930
If you still have the energy to say "no,"
you still have the energy to do it!

00:10:53.110 --> 00:10:56.100
What's the point of all
this training, anyway?

00:10:56.280 --> 00:11:00.270
In your current state, there's no way you'll
be able to handle Miyuki's "Today."

00:11:01.350 --> 00:11:04.220
What have I done
to deserve this?

00:11:04.380 --> 00:11:06.850
Alrighty! As soon as you're finished
here, we're off for a run!

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:09.420
What?! There's
more?!

00:11:09.990 --> 00:11:11.890
Let me call
it quits!

00:11:13.430 --> 00:11:15.390
Poor Yoriko!

00:11:33.850 --> 00:11:35.910
Poor Yoriko. I hope
she'll be okay.

00:11:36.080 --> 00:11:38.450
She'll be just
fine.

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:41.480
Anyway, she has us
to cheer her on!

00:11:41.650 --> 00:11:42.680
Precisely!

00:11:46.630 --> 00:11:49.150
All ready!

00:11:49.700 --> 00:11:51.250
"Cheer her on?"

00:11:57.240 --> 00:12:00.260
Ah! Today's going to be the
best day of my entire life.

00:12:00.740 --> 00:12:04.270
I've read my tea leaves and gotten
a fortune from the temple...

00:12:04.810 --> 00:12:08.250
Even my horoscope
confirmed it!

00:12:08.350 --> 00:12:13.250
But why is Yoriko so
late getting here?!

00:12:13.350 --> 00:12:16.380
Look at the time. Maybe
she's read...

00:12:16.490 --> 00:12:19.460
"Musashi and Kojiro" - legendary
Japanese samurai.
...Musashi Miyamoto
and Kojiro Sasaki...

00:12:19.630 --> 00:12:22.600
...so she's late on purpose!
Figures.

00:12:27.400 --> 00:12:31.000
Sorry! Sorry to keep
you waiting!

00:12:31.170 --> 00:12:36.010
Yoriko, you came late just to get me upset,
but let me assure you, it didn't work.

00:12:36.540 --> 00:12:39.910
No. I just got caught
in traffic, that's all.

00:12:40.080 --> 00:12:42.950
Caught in
traffic?!

00:12:43.050 --> 00:12:46.080
Well, in that case, you
should've left earlier!

00:12:46.250 --> 00:12:49.220
Hey, Chie, looks like I did
get you upset after all!

00:12:56.060 --> 00:12:58.220
The person who can nab the
most traffic violators...

00:12:58.330 --> 00:13:02.130
...and cite them for demerit points
by 5;00 is the winner. Got it?

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:03.390
OK, I guess...

00:13:03.570 --> 00:13:06.040
Then we'll start as soon as
the light turns green.

00:13:19.820 --> 00:13:22.450
Look at that, that's
really dangerous.

00:13:22.560 --> 00:13:24.790
It won't be funny if she
gets in an accident!

00:13:24.960 --> 00:13:28.090
Hey! What are you doing?! Hurry
up and go after the Porsche!

00:13:28.260 --> 00:13:31.560
Huh? Is that you,
Natsumi?!

00:13:31.730 --> 00:13:34.670
We set up a camera in the car
so we can cheer you on!

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:37.730
Come on! You've got to hurry!
Otherwise you'll lose for sure!

00:13:37.900 --> 00:13:41.470
Natsumi, don't be pushing her so
hard, or she'll have an accident.

00:13:42.180 --> 00:13:45.340
Yoriko! Don't pay any attention
to what Natsumi says!

00:13:45.510 --> 00:13:46.410
Okay.

00:13:53.050 --> 00:13:56.850
That slow little tortoise of a car
versus my hare of a Porsche!

00:13:56.960 --> 00:14:01.390
Well, I'm not as silly as the
hare in the fable! Huh?

00:14:03.830 --> 00:14:05.820
What? I don't
believe it!

00:14:10.970 --> 00:14:13.440
Yes! Come on, baby!
She's going for it!

00:14:13.610 --> 00:14:14.470
Yoriko!

00:14:14.470 --> 00:14:16.810
Yoriko!
Miyuki! Yoriko's doing okay! Huh?

00:14:20.180 --> 00:14:21.410
What's that?

00:14:21.580 --> 00:14:23.140
The remote control
for the car.

00:14:23.320 --> 00:14:25.180
"Remote control?!"
"Remote control?!"

00:14:25.350 --> 00:14:28.050
I thought things might turn out this
way, so I installed it just in case.

00:14:30.590 --> 00:14:34.030
What's going on? The steering
wheel is turning all by itself!

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:42.970
Oh, oh no!

00:14:48.810 --> 00:14:50.740
I get it! You're doing this, Miyuki!

00:14:50.740 --> 00:14:53.300
I get it! You're doing this, Miyuki!
Just keep quiet.

00:15:00.450 --> 00:15:03.580
Unbelievable! I'm not gonna
let her beat me!

00:15:18.340 --> 00:15:22.170
Yoriko! Are you okay?
Come in! Yoriko!

00:15:22.340 --> 00:15:24.470
I'm starting to feel
a lot better now.

00:15:24.640 --> 00:15:29.210
I'm sorry. I got a little carried away
when Chie called my car a tortoise.

00:15:29.380 --> 00:15:33.680
Yoriko! Stop slacking! Get out there and
nail people, or Chie's gonna crush you!

00:15:33.850 --> 00:15:36.580
Yeah, yeah. I
know. Oh.

00:15:37.790 --> 00:15:39.530
Y... Yoriko, what're you doing?! Stop!

00:15:39.530 --> 00:15:40.760
It's all this thing's fault!

00:15:40.760 --> 00:15:42.460
Stop that! Hey!

00:15:42.630 --> 00:15:43.560
Oops.

00:15:45.300 --> 00:15:48.530
Ooh! All I was doing was
trying to help you!

00:15:48.700 --> 00:15:52.030
If the car drives itself, I'll have to
use up more than a few lives.

00:15:52.340 --> 00:15:55.310
Sorry! But this is something that
I'd rather try to do on my own.

00:16:00.050 --> 00:16:02.910
What is it? Someone passing
illegally? A souped up car?

00:16:03.080 --> 00:16:06.050
Nope. Kindergartners trying
to use a crosswalk.

00:16:12.190 --> 00:16:13.560
You can
cross!

00:16:13.660 --> 00:16:15.630
Take your time,
kids!

00:16:20.170 --> 00:16:22.630
Ah, this is a
good patch.

00:16:28.740 --> 00:16:31.010
That's terrible!
The fiend!

00:16:42.320 --> 00:16:44.620
I don't let my prey get
away from me.

00:16:50.100 --> 00:16:53.550
Two points for running a red. Six points
for going 30km over the speed limit.

00:16:56.240 --> 00:16:59.330
Aha! Looks like we can add
illegal passing to the list!

00:16:59.440 --> 00:17:02.410
So two more points, bringing
the grand total to 10!

00:17:10.020 --> 00:17:13.180
Well, what do you know! I can find
traffic violators with this thing!

00:17:13.350 --> 00:17:18.450
Uh, oh, Chie's really going full bore,
and she's about to catch someone.

00:17:18.620 --> 00:17:20.560
Yoriko! Yoriko!

00:17:20.730 --> 00:17:21.290
Take care now!

00:17:21.290 --> 00:17:23.260
Thanks, I will.

00:17:25.100 --> 00:17:28.070
Thank you very much
for waiting.

00:17:33.040 --> 00:17:36.910
What on earth are you doing?! Chie's
chasing down an offender!

00:17:37.340 --> 00:17:40.610
But this is an important part of
being a police officer, too!

00:17:40.980 --> 00:17:42.950
Yoriko's great!

00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:44.740
But right now she's
trying to win a race!

00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:48.220
Yoriko! I've found you
someone to catch!

00:17:51.220 --> 00:17:52.990
Just follow my
instructions.

00:17:53.160 --> 00:17:54.250
Roger!

00:17:54.430 --> 00:17:56.990
Turn right at the next
intersection.

00:18:00.370 --> 00:18:02.860
Left at the
next light.

00:18:06.070 --> 00:18:07.600
Found him!

00:18:07.710 --> 00:18:08.610
Oh!

00:18:08.740 --> 00:18:09.710
What happened?

00:18:09.710 --> 00:18:11.540
What happened?
What's wrong? What is it?

00:18:11.710 --> 00:18:15.610
There's an old woman who's trying
to cross the road, but can't do it!

00:18:16.450 --> 00:18:16.580
Take your time now. That's right.

00:18:16.580 --> 00:18:18.550
What a good girl you are.

00:18:18.550 --> 00:18:21.110
It's hard to cross here, isn't it?

00:18:22.990 --> 00:18:26.620
This sucks. She's never going
to be able to give out a ticket.

00:18:27.190 --> 00:18:29.090
But I think that's
fine.

00:18:29.630 --> 00:18:34.090
Why? That means she'll lose
to that stuck-up bitch!

00:18:35.570 --> 00:18:41.600
Chie thinks that being a police officer
simply means handing out tickets.

00:18:41.710 --> 00:18:47.610
But when you think about it, it's
so, so much more than that!

00:19:08.570 --> 00:19:13.130
Yes, you're right. Protecting children
and the elderly from traffic...

00:19:13.240 --> 00:19:15.370
...is also an important
part of police duty.

00:19:15.810 --> 00:19:19.270
That's right! And I think it's some-
thing that Yoriko is suited for.

00:19:20.080 --> 00:19:23.780
And as far as traffic violators go, well,
you and I can take care of them.

00:19:23.950 --> 00:19:27.650
We sure can. Even
Yoriko's share!

00:19:28.390 --> 00:19:30.150
Kobayakawa! Tsuji-
moto! Aoi!

00:19:30.920 --> 00:19:33.150
Huh?

00:19:36.230 --> 00:19:39.130
Well, Yoriko? How many demerit
points did you rack up?

00:19:39.230 --> 00:19:41.790
I have a total
of 54!

00:19:41.970 --> 00:19:43.940
I didn't get any
points.

00:19:45.270 --> 00:19:49.800
Just as I expected. Of course, my
abilities far exceed your own.

00:19:49.910 --> 00:19:52.500
There's no way you could
have won against me.

00:19:52.610 --> 00:19:56.510
You just happened to get lucky
back at the police academy...

00:19:56.620 --> 00:19:58.240
...and it was just a fluke
that you beat me!

00:19:58.420 --> 00:20:01.390
But I didn't think
that...

00:20:15.400 --> 00:20:19.000
I'm sorry. You guys went to a lot of
trouble to help me, and I still lost.

00:20:19.170 --> 00:20:20.170
What are you saying?!

00:20:20.170 --> 00:20:21.700
What are you saying?!
You did great, Yoriko!

00:20:21.870 --> 00:20:22.640
Huh?

00:20:22.640 --> 00:20:24.670
Huh?
Way to go, Yoriko!

00:20:24.840 --> 00:20:25.810
What?!

00:20:28.280 --> 00:20:33.280
<i>I've knocked Yoriko down a few pegs, and</i>
<i>avenged my humiliation at the academy...</i>

00:20:33.450 --> 00:20:33.590
<i>So, there's no reason</i>
<i>why I should stay.</i>

00:20:33.590 --> 00:20:36.280
"Notice of Resignation"
<i>So, there's no reason</i>
<i>why I should stay.</i>

00:20:39.190 --> 00:20:42.160
<i>Once I submit this, I'll leave</i>
<i>as an able officer...</i>

00:20:42.260 --> 00:20:46.160
<i>... and make my big debut</i>
<i>as a princess of justice!</i>

00:20:46.570 --> 00:20:50.300
Hey, did you hear? Yoriko Nikaidou
from the Bokuto Station...

00:20:50.400 --> 00:20:52.870
...is going to receive a special commen-
dation for her courteous behavior.

00:20:53.040 --> 00:20:54.340
Really?

00:20:54.510 --> 00:20:57.310
Wait! Hold it! Hang on a sec!
What did you just say?!

00:20:57.480 --> 00:21:02.780
The Chief happened to see her escort
a group of kids across a street...

00:21:03.120 --> 00:21:06.780
"Although we commend all those who
work to solve various crimes...

00:21:06.890 --> 00:21:08.380
"...it is felt that we must
also commend...

00:21:08.490 --> 00:21:10.790
"...those who work to help maintain
the good relationship...

00:21:10.890 --> 00:21:13.420
"...between the police department
and the local community."

00:21:13.530 --> 00:21:17.760
"As such, I award you the 1st Special
Service Commendation."

00:21:18.100 --> 00:21:22.090
"Signed; Daizaburo Tokumaru,
Chief of Police."

00:21:28.840 --> 00:21:34.680
<i>Yoriko, if you've won the Chief's 1st</i>
<i>Special Service Commendation...</i>

00:21:35.210 --> 00:21:40.480
...then I'll win the Chief's Official
Commendation for Excellence!

00:21:42.290 --> 00:21:45.920
I wonder if I really
deserve this?

00:21:46.090 --> 00:21:47.130
Congratulations!

00:21:47.130 --> 00:21:52.120
Congratulations!
Great! Way to go!

00:22:02.410 --> 00:22:10.980
<i>I live my life my own way, doing</i>
<i>things others wouldn't.</i>

00:22:11.250 --> 00:22:19.550
<i>Being strong isn't enough.</i>
<i>It makes me Ionely.</i>

00:22:22.290 --> 00:22:30.600
<i>I can feel your presence</i>
<i>as if you're right here...</i>

00:22:31.140 --> 00:22:38.710
<i>... but I can't say a word.</i>

00:22:40.250 --> 00:22:47.490
<i>The feelings I hide within might</i>
<i>break into pieces...</i>

00:22:48.990 --> 00:22:56.400
<i>But if I don't say anything,</i>
<i>nothing can begin.</i>

00:22:56.700 --> 00:23:03.930
<i>The wind gently blows...</i>
<i>Time flows...</i>

00:23:08.910 --> 00:23:10.910
<i>Time flows... And soon</i>
<i>I can be honest...</i>

00:23:16.050 --> 00:23:16.740
<i>Thank you,</i>
<i>friend!</i>

00:23:23.020 --> 00:23:25.180
"Focus of Suspicion"

00:23:25.290 --> 00:23:26.950
Have you seen Nakajima
anywhere?

00:23:27.130 --> 00:23:29.460
He must be hiding somewhere,
reading some porn...

00:23:29.630 --> 00:23:31.360
Ah... Speaking of Nakajima...

00:23:31.360 --> 00:23:32.500
What's on your mind?

00:23:32.500 --> 00:23:33.800
Guess what, he's cheating!

00:23:33.800 --> 00:23:35.740
He'd be the last person to cheat!

00:23:35.740 --> 00:23:37.500
No, his kind are always cheaters!

00:23:37.500 --> 00:23:39.160
Hey, hey, what's going on?

00:23:39.340 --> 00:23:42.470
The man in question is here. Who
is it that you're going out with?

00:23:42.640 --> 00:23:44.230
Hey, I don't know what
you're talking about!

00:23:44.410 --> 00:23:47.580
Next time on You're Under Arrest,
File 9, "The Love Triangle."

00:23:47.710 --> 00:23:49.720
Oh, give me
a break!
